    {
      "Name": "Silicon carbide (4H, semi-insulating)",
      "Epsr": 9.7,
      "TanD": 0.0005,
      "Mur": 1,
      "ThermalK": 383,
      "ThermalKVsTemp": [
        { "TempC": 20, "Value": 383 },
        { "TempC": 50, "Value": 331 },
        { "TempC": 100, "Value": 266.7 },
        { "TempC": 150, "Value": 220.9 },
        { "TempC": 200, "Value": 186.8 },
        { "TempC": 250, "Value": 160.7 },
        { "TempC": 300, "Value": 140.1 },
        { "TempC": 400, "Value": 110.1 },
        { "TempC": 500, "Value": 89.43 }
      ],
      "DensityKgM3": 3210,
      "SpecificHeat": 690,
      "Source": "Relative permittivity 9.7: 4H-SiC's static value is 9.66 perpendicular to the c axis and 10.03 along it (Levinshtein, Rumyantsev and Shur (eds.), Properties of Advanced Semiconductor Materials, Wiley, 2001); 9.7 is the value commonly used for a c-plane substrate. It holds from DC to well above 100 GHz: the lattice resonance that ends it is in the infrared. Loss tangent 0.0005: a representative value for a semi-insulating wafer at microwave frequencies, not a measurement - replace with the supplier's figure. Thermal conductivity k(T) = k300 (T / 300 K)^-1.5 with k300 = 370 W/(m K), tabulated 20 to 500 C: k300 from Levinshtein, Rumyantsev and Shur (eds.), Properties of Advanced Semiconductor Materials: GaN, AlN, InN, BN, SiC, SiGe (Wiley, 2001), 3.7 W/(cm K) for 4H-SiC at 300 K; the exponent is of the size reported for SiC above room temperature (about 1.3 to 1.6). Semi-insulating wafers measure roughly 330 to 490 W/(m K) at room temperature by growth and doping: replace with the supplier's figure. Density 3210 kg/m3 and specific heat 690 J/(kg K): same source. Representative, not a measurement.",
      "Color": "#5f7f6a"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Gallium nitride",
      "Epsr": 9.5,
      "TanD": 0.001,
      "Mur": 1,
      "ThermalK": 165.3,
      "ThermalKVsTemp": [
        { "TempC": 20, "Value": 165.3 },
        { "TempC": 50, "Value": 144.2 },
